<section id="faq">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<FaqItem question="Which AI tool should I start with?">
<p>Canva AI (free tier). Every article you publish needs images — header graphics, product screenshots, comparison visuals, social share images. Canva's AI features let you create these without design skills, and the free plan covers the volume most beginners need. After that, add an AI writing tool when your publishing frequency justifies the time savings.</p>
</FaqItem>

<FaqItem question="Do I need all of these tools?">
<p>No. The recommended stack (Canva + SEO Writing AI + FastBots + Surfer + HeyGen) covers five different workflows — design, writing, chatbot, SEO, and video. Most affiliate marketers get strong results from the first 2–3 tools. Add tools when a specific bottleneck appears, not because a tool exists.</p>
</FaqItem>

<FaqItem question="Are AI-generated reviews and articles allowed by Google?">
<p>Google's guidelines state that content should be helpful, reliable, and people-first — regardless of how it was produced. AI-generated content is not automatically penalised. However, unedited AI content that lacks originality, expertise, or trustworthiness signals (EEAT) typically underperforms human-edited content. The approach we recommend — AI for drafting and research, human for editing, structure, and originality — consistently produces content that meets Google's quality standards.</p>
</FaqItem>

<FaqItem question="How much do these AI tools cost per month?">
<p>Starting from zero: Canva (free), SEO Writing AI (free for 3 articles), FastBots (free for 25 messages/month). Total: $0/month for a functional beginner stack. The paid stack — Canva Pro ($13), SEO Writing AI paid tier (~$29), FastBots paid (~$19), Surfer SEO ($49), HeyGen ($29) — totals approximately $139/month. Most affiliates add tools gradually as revenue increases, not all at once.</p>
</FaqItem>

<FaqItem question="How are these reviews produced?">
<p>All AI tool reviews on Profit and Privilege follow the same research-backed methodology: we analyse the tool's public documentation, feature lists, pricing pages, and independent user reports. We verify claims where possible, distinguish vendor statements from independently confirmed facts, and disclose what we could not verify. No hands-on testing is claimed unless explicitly stated. We earn affiliate commissions from some tools reviewed here — these relationships are disclosed in each review and do not influence our editorial assessment. For more detail, see each review's methodology section.</p>
</FaqItem>
